    "title": "Overdue serum creatinine monitoring on TDF",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR every 12 months for experienced patients on TDF. The patient's only creatinine result is from 2024-10-01, approximately 15 months ago, making it overdue. TDF can cause chronic kidney disease, acute kidney injury, and Fanconi syndrome. No current symptoms or examination findings suggest renal toxicity, and the prior creatinine of 88 umol/L was normal. However, the absence of recent renal function tests means any decline since October 2024 would be undetected. The clinician's plan does not include renal function testing.",
